---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Why Spacefast?"
  description="Give what your agent makes a home on the web with Spacefast."
>
  <article class="article">
    <header>
      <h1>Your idea called. It wants a URL.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        That thing you made in a chat deserves somewhere to live.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This is a demo of <strong>Small Internet</strong>, an editable Astro
        theme with three hand-drawn looks. Spacefast is the sample subject;
        change the writing and links to make the theme yours. It runs as a
        standard static Astro site on your chosen host.
      </p>
      <p>
        A page for your club. A game for your friends. A gloriously specific
        guide to something you love. Spacefast gives your agent’s creations a
        home on the web.
      </p>
      <h2>Make it. Then let it out.</h2>
      <p>
        Ask your agent to publish with Spacefast, or choose a publishing route
        that fits your workflow. Static sites and supported full-stack apps have
        a place here. Check the{' '}
        <a href="https://spacefast.com/docs/">current docs</a> for your
        project’s requirements.
      </p>
      <h2>Your audience, your call.</h2>
      <p>
        New spaces start private. Invite people, create a viewer link, or make
        your space public when you’re ready. A private URL alone does not grant
        access.
      </p>
      <h2>Keep the link. Change the thing.</h2>
      <p>
        Republish at the same address as your creation grows. Each change saves
        a version; you can restore a version still in your history.
      </p>
      <h2>A small invitation.</h2>
      <p>
        Pick one idea you keep talking about. Make a useful first version. Give
        it a home. The little oddball believes in you.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="article-end">
      <a class="button" href="https://spacefast.com/">
        Meet Spacefast ↗
      </a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
